node_modules
dist
dev-dist
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo
.vite
*.local
.DS_Store

# Tooling metadata (a project id), not part of the app.
.freebuff/

# Rust / Tauri: any build cache (cargo's is per-workspace, and a nested one
# appears if a command is run from inside a member crate), plus the ACL schemas
# generated at build time. The workspace root Cargo.lock *is* committed: this is
# an application, not a library.
target/
src-tauri/gen/schemas

# An assembled macOS bundle, if `src-tauri/macos/bundle.mjs` is run here rather
# than on the runner that ships it. The directory-only form keeps a file that
# merely ends in `.app` visible.
*.app/

# The rest of `src-tauri/gen` is *not* ignored: `tauri android init` writes the
# Gradle project the APK is built from into `gen/android`, and that is meant to
# be committed. It carries its own `.gitignore` for the Gradle caches it makes.
